<!doctype html>
<html lang='en'>
<head>
  <meta charset='utf-8'>
  <meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1'>
  <title>{{ title }}</title>
  <style>
    @page { size: A4 landscape; margin: 14mm; }
    :root { --ink: #172033; --muted: #596579; --line: #d8dee8; --teal: #145a64; --gold: #d69e2e; --red: #a94442; --paper: #ffffff; --wash: #f6f8fb; }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body { margin: 0; background: var(--wash); color: var(--ink); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; }
    main { max-width: 1320px; margin: 0 auto; background: var(--paper); padding: 34px 42px 48px; }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: 0; }
    h2 { margin: 30px 0 12px; padding-bottom: 7px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--teal); font-size: 20px; }
    h3 { margin: 22px 0 8px; font-size: 15px; }
    p { margin: 7px 0; }
    .subtitle { color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; }
    .warning { margin: 20px 0; padding: 14px 16px; border-left: 5px solid var(--red); background: #fff4f2; font-weight: 600; }
    .metrics { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin: 20px 0; }
    .metric { flex: 1 1 150px; min-width: 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-top: 3px solid var(--gold); padding: 11px 12px; min-height: 78px; }
    .metric strong { display: block; font-size: 20px; }
    .metric span { color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; }
    .figure { margin: 15px 0 24px; page-break-inside: avoid; }
    .figure img { width: 100%; max-height: 700px; object-fit: contain; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .caption { color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; margin-top: 4px; }
    .table-wrap { margin: 10px 0 22px; }
    table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 11px; }
    th { background: #e9f0f2; color: #233447; text-align: right; padding: 7px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
    th:first-child, td:first-child { text-align: left; }
    td { text-align: right; padding: 6px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
    tr:nth-child(even) td { background: #fafbfc; }
    .two { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 20px; }
    .two > * { flex: 1 1 380px; min-width: 0; }
    .method { padding: 12px 14px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: #fbfcfe; }
    .method strong { color: var(--teal); }
    .interpretation { margin: 10px 0 16px; padding: 10px 13px; border-left: 4px solid var(--gold); background: #fbfcfe; }
    .footnote { color: var(--muted); font-size: 10px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
  <p class='subtitle'>Net USD evidence for every current portfolio output, regional index benchmarks, and an independent point-in-time index challenger.</p>
  <div class='warning'>{{ warning }}</div>
  <div class='metrics'>
    <div class='metric'><strong>{{ strategy_count }}</strong><span>portfolio outputs tested</span></div>
    <div class='metric'><strong>{{ requested_years }}</strong><span>requested historical years</span></div>
    <div class='metric'><strong>{{ current_nav }}</strong><span>current-derived starting NAV</span></div>
    <div class='metric'><strong>{{ common_start }}</strong><span>common 80% investable start</span></div>
    <div class='metric'><strong>{{ pit_months }}</strong><span>separate reconstructed PIT months</span></div>
    <div class='metric'><strong>{{ benchmark_count }}</strong><span>standalone benchmark paths</span></div>
    <div class='metric'><strong>{{ event_count }}</strong><span>source-backed macro-event windows</span></div>
  </div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.overall }}</p>

  <h2>Executive Comparison</h2>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ performance_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.executive }}</p>
  <div class='figure'><img src='plots/wealth_paths.png' alt='Portfolio wealth paths'><p class='caption'>Indexed growth uses each portfolio's assigned capital only for PnL; this chart rebases every series to 100 for comparability.</p></div>
  <div class='two'>
    <div class='figure'><img src='plots/ending_pnl.png' alt='Ending PnL'></div>
    <div class='figure'><img src='plots/risk_return.png' alt='Risk and return'></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Paper Ratios and Annual Bank Charge</h2>
  <h3>Performance Ratios on the Common Investable Window</h3>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ ratio_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.ratios }}</p>
  <h3>Annual Fee Assumption</h3>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ fee_assumption_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.fee_assumption }}</p>
  <h3>Fee Impact by Portfolio</h3>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ fee_impact_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.fee_impact }}</p>

  <h2>Major Index Benchmarks</h2>
  <div class='figure'><img src='plots/benchmark_comparison.png' alt='Index benchmark comparison'><p class='caption'>Dashed lines are broad or regional index benchmarks. Portfolio-specific relative statistics use each allocation's geographic index blend on the common investable window.</p></div>
  <div class='figure'><img src='plots/major_indices.png' alt='Major index benchmarks in USD'></div>
  <h3>Standalone Index Performance, Common Investable Window</h3>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ benchmark_performance_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.benchmarks }}</p>
  <div class='figure'><img src='plots/drawdowns.png' alt='Drawdowns'></div>
  <div class='figure'><img src='plots/annual_returns.png' alt='Annual return heatmap'></div>
  <h3>Portfolio-Relative Regional Benchmark Results</h3>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ benchmark_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.relative_benchmarks }}</p>

  <h2>Interest Rates and Market Regimes</h2>
  <div class='figure'><img src='plots/interest_rate_history.png' alt='Interest-rate history'></div>
  <h3>Interest-Rate Level Performance</h3>
  <div class='figure'><img src='plots/interest_rate_performance.png' alt='Performance across interest-rate levels'></div>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ rate_level_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.rate_level }}</p>
  <h3>Interest-Rate Direction Performance</h3>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ rate_direction_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.rate_direction }}</p>
  <h3>Lagged Market Regime Performance</h3>
  <div class='figure'><img src='plots/market_regime_performance.png' alt='Performance across market regimes'></div>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ market_regime_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.market_regime }}</p>
  <h3>Retrospective Economic-Cycle Performance</h3>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ economic_cycle_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.economic_cycle }}</p>

  <h2>Major Macro Events</h2>
  <div class='figure'><img src='plots/macro_event_timeline.png' alt='Wealth through major macro events'><p class='caption'>Shading includes the Asian crisis, dot-com bust, global financial crisis, COVID-19, political shocks, and war windows through the 2026 US-Iran conflict.</p></div>
  <div class='figure'><img src='plots/macro_event_returns.png' alt='Returns during macro-event windows'></div>
  <h3>Configured Event Windows</h3>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ event_definition_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.event_definitions }}</p>
  <h3>Portfolio and S&amp;P 500 Event Performance</h3>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ event_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.events }}</p>

  <h2>The Three Backtests</h2>
  <div class='two'>
    <div class='method'><strong>1. Historical / walk-forward</strong><p>Monthly execution with one-period signal lag for the index challenger. Current portfolio outputs are shown only as retrospective holdings replays and are explicitly flagged for selection look-ahead and survivorship bias.</p></div>
    <div class='method'><strong>2. Resampling</strong><p>Circular 12-month moving blocks preserve serial dependence and cross-strategy alignment. The intervals show how path order changes CAGR, Sharpe, drawdown, and benchmark outperformance.</p></div>
    <div class='method'><strong>3. Monte Carlo</strong><p>A correlated Student-t AR(1) process with EWMA conditional variance preserves cross-portfolio dependence, autocorrelation, fat tails, and volatility clustering without fitting a return target.</p></div>
    <div class='method'><strong>Statistical integrity</strong><p>PSR, MinTRL, Sidak family-wise control, and Deflated Sharpe Ratios account for sample length, non-normal returns, and the number and correlation of portfolio trials.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class='two'>
    <div class='figure'><img src='plots/block_resampling.png' alt='Block bootstrap intervals'></div>
    <div class='figure'><img src='plots/monte_carlo.png' alt='Monte Carlo intervals'></div>
  </div>
  <h3>Moving-Block Resampling Summary</h3>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ resampling_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.resampling }}</p>
  <h3>Monte Carlo Summary</h3>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ monte_carlo_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.monte_carlo }}</p>
  <h3>Untouched Embargo Comparison</h3>
  <div class='figure'><img src='plots/embargo.png' alt='Embargo comparison'></div>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ embargo_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.embargo }}</p>
  <h3>Statistical Significance and Multiple Testing</h3>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ significance_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.significance }}</p>
  <h3>Alpha and Strategy-Selection Overfitting</h3>
  <div class='figure'><img src='plots/alpha_significance.png' alt='Matched-benchmark alpha significance'></div>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ overfitting_table }}</div>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ reality_check_table }}</div>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ alpha_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.alpha_overfitting }}</p>

  <h2>Data Quality and Causality</h2>
  <h3>Execution and Liquidity</h3>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ execution_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.execution }}</p>
  <h3>Adjusted-Price Repairs</h3>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ repair_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.repairs }}</p>
  <div class='figure'><img src='plots/investable_starts.png' alt='Investable starts'></div>
  <div class='figure'><img src='plots/causal_graph.png' alt='Causal graph'></div>
  <h3>Bias and Limitation Register</h3>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ limitation_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.limitations }}</p>

  <h2>Point-in-Time Model Evidence</h2>
  <p>The repository's reconstructed model walk-forward is not spliced into the 1997 holdings replay. It remains a separate, shorter evidence set because it uses dated model decisions and realised outcomes.</p>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ pit_table }}</div>
  <h3>Point-in-Time Alpha Tests</h3>
  <div class='table-wrap'>{{ pit_alpha_table }}</div>
  <p class='interpretation'>{{ interpretations.pit }}</p>

  <p class='footnote'>Research evidence only. The paper used as the methodological specification is <em>The Three Types of Backtests</em> (Joubert, Sestovic, Barziy, Distaso, and Lopez de Prado, 29 July 2024). Raw Yahoo Finance and FRED histories remain outside Git; compact outputs, manifests, and checksums are included.</p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
